<title>BANGLADESH: Burma frees 19 Bangladeshi fishermen.</title>
<headline>Burma frees 19 Bangladeshi fishermen.</headline>
<dateline>COX'S BAZAR, Bangladesh 1997-02-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Burma on Sunday released 19 Bangladeshi fishermen detained by its border guards in December, officials said.</p>
<p>They said the 19 and their boats were seized by Burmese border guards on the border river Naf for allegedly entering Burmese waters.</p>
<p>The Bangladeshis denied the charge.</p>
<p>&quot;Their release followed a meeting between border guards of the two countries at the Burmese town of Maungdaw on Sunday,&quot; one official told reporters.</p>
<p>&quot;Over 100 more fishermen forcibly taken into Burma over last few months are still there and we are trying to obtain their freedom,&quot; he said without giving details.</p>
</text>
